H1800.definition:
from H1809 (דָּלַל);
properly, dangling, i.e. (by implication) weak or thin
KJV: lean, needy, poor (man), weaker.

H1801.definition:
a primitive root;
to spring
KJV: leap.

H1802.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1809 (דָּלַל));
properly, to dangle, i.e. to let down abucket (for drawing out water); figuratively, to deliver
KJV: draw (out), [idiom] enough, lift up.

H1803.definition:
from H1802 (דָּלָה);
properly, something dangling, i.e. a loose thread or hair; figuratively, indigent
KJV: hair, pining sickness, poor(-est sort).

H1804.definition:
a primitive root;
to roil water
KJV: trouble.

H1805.definition:
or דֳּלִי; from H1802 (דָּלָה);
a pail or jar (for drawing water)
KJV: bucket.

H1806.definition:
or (prolonged) דְּלָיָהוּxlit Dᵉlâyâhhûw corrected to Dᵉlâyâhûw; from H1802 (דָּלָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has delivered;
Delajah, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Dalaiah, Delaiah.

H1808.definition:
from H1802 (דָּלָה);
something dangling, i.e. a bough
KJV: branch.

H1809.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1802 (דָּלָה));
to slacken or be feeble; figuratively, to be oppressed
KJV: bring low, dry up, be emptied, be not equal, fail, be impoverished, be made thin.

H1810.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Dilan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dilean.

H1811.definition:
a primitive root;
to drip; by implication, to weep
KJV: drop through, melt, pour out.

H1812.definition:
from H1811 (דָּלַף);
a dripping
KJV: dropping.

H1813.definition:
from H1811 (דָּלַף); dripping;
Dalphon, a son of Haman
KJV: Dalphon.

H1814.definition:
a primitive root;
to flame (literally or figuratively)
KJV: burning, chase, inflame, kindle, persecute(-or), pursue hotly.

H1815.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1814 (דָּלַק)
{to flame (literally or figuratively)}
KJV: burn.

H1816.definition:
; from H1814 (דָּלַק);
a burning fever
KJV: inflammation.

H1817.definition:
from H1802 (דָּלָה);
something swinging, i.e. the valve of adoor
KJV: door (two-leaved), gate, leaf, lid. (Psalm 141:3).

H1818.definition:
from H1826 (דָּמַם) (compare H119 (אָדַם));
blood (as that which when shed causes death) of man or an animal; by analogy, the juice of the grape; figuratively (especially in the plural) bloodshed (i.e. drops of blood)
KJV: blood(-y, -guiltiness, (-thirsty), [phrase] innocent.

H1819.definition:
a primitive root;
to compare; by implication, to resemble, liken, consider
KJV: compare, devise, (be) like(-n), mean, think, use similitudes.

H1820.definition:
a primitive root;
to be dumb or silent; hence, to fail or perish; trans. to destroy
KJV: cease, be cut down (off), destroy, be brought to silence, be undone, [idiom] utterly.

H1821.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1819 (דָּמָה);
to resemble
KJV: be like.

H1822.definition:
from H1820 (דָּמָה);
desolation; concretely, desolate
KJV: destroy.

H1823.definition:
from H1819 (דָּמָה);
resemblance; concretely, model, shape; adverbially, like
KJV: fashion, like (-ness, as), manner, similitude.

H1824.definition:
or דֳּמִי; from H1820 (דָּמָה);
quiet
KJV: cutting off, rest, silence.

H1826.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1724 (דָּהַם), H1820 (דָּמָה));
to be dumb; by implication, to be astonished, to stop; also to perish
KJV: cease, be cut down (off), forbear, hold peace, quiet self, rest, be silent, keep (put to) silence, be (stand) still, tarry, wait.

H1827.definition:
feminine from H1826 (דָּמַם);
quiet
KJV: calm, silence, still.

H1828.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
manure
KJV: dung.

H1829.definition:
feminine from the same as H1828 (דֹּמֶן); a dung-heap;
Dimnah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dimnah.

H1830.definition:
a primitive root;
to weep
KJV: [idiom] sore, weep.

H1831.definition:
from H1830 (דָּמַע);
a tear; figuratively, juice
KJV: liquor.

H1832.definition:
feminine of H1831 (דֶּמַע);
weeping
KJV: tears.

H1833.definition:
by orthographical variation from H1834 (דַּמֶּשֶׂק);
damask (as a fabric of Damascus)
KJV: in Damascus.

H1834.definition:
or דּוּמֶשֶׂק; or דַּרְמֶשֶׂק; of foreign origin;
Damascus, a city of Syria
KJV: Damascus.

H1835.definition:
from H1777 (דִּין); judge;
Dan, one of the sons of Jacob; also the tribe descended from him, and its territory; likewise a place in Palestine colonized by them
KJV: Daniel

H1836.definition:
(Aramaic) an orthographical variation of H1791 (דֵּךְ);
this
KJV: (afore-) time, [phrase] after this manner, here (-after), one...another, such, there(-fore), these, this (matter), [phrase] thus, where(-fore), which.

H1837.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Dannah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dannah.

H1838.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Dinhabah, an Edomitish town
KJV: Dinhaban.

H1839.definition:
patronymically from H1835 (דָּן);
a Danite (often collectively) or descendants (or inhabitants) of Dan
KJV: Danites, of Daniel

H1840.definition:
in Ezekiel it is; דָּנִאֵל; from H1835 (דָּן) and H410 (אֵל); judge of God;
Daniel or Danijel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Daniel.

H1841.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1840 (דָנִיֵּאל);
Danijel, the Hebrew prophet
KJV: Daniel.

H1842.definition:
from H1835 (דָּן) and (apparently) H3282 (יַעַן); judge of purpose;
Dan-Jaan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dan-jaan.

H1843.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע);
knowledge
KJV: knowledge, opinion.

H1844.definition:
feminine of H1843 (דֵּעַ);
knowledge
KJV: knowledge.

H1845.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע) and H410 (אֵל); known of God;
Deuel, an Israelite
KJV: Deuel.

H1846.definition:
a primitive root;
to be extinguished; figuratively, to expire or be dried up
KJV: be extinct, consumed, put out, quenched.

H1847.definition:
from H3045 (יָדַע);
knowledge
KJV: cunning, (ig-) norantly, know(-ledge), (un-) awares (wittingly).

H1848.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to push over);
a stumbling-block
KJV: slanderest.

H1849.definition:
a primitive root;
to knock; by analogy, to press severely
KJV: beat, knock, overdrive.

H1850.definition:
from H1849 (דָּפַק); a knock;
Dophkah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Dophkah.

H1851.definition:
from H1854 (דָּקַק);
crushed, i.e. (by implication) small or thin
KJV: dwarf, lean(-fleshed), very little thing, small, thin.

H1852.definition:
from H1854 (דָּקַק);
something crumbling, i.e. fine (as a thin cloth)
KJV: curtain.

H1853.definition:
of foreign origin;
Diklah, a region of Arabia
KJV: Diklah.

H1854.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1915 (הָדַךְ)lemma הָדךְ missing vowel, corrected to הָדַךְ);
to crush (or intransitively) crumble
KJV: beat in pieces (small), bruise, make dust, (into) [idiom] powder, (be, very) small, stamp (small).

H1855.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1854 (דָּקַק);
to crumble or (trans.) crush
KJV: break to pieces.

H1856.definition:
a primitive root;
to stab; by analogy, to starve; figuratively, to revile
KJV: pierce, strike (thrust) through, wound.

H1857.definition:
from H1856 (דָּקַר); a stab;
Deker, an Israelite
KJV: Dekar.

H1858.definition:
apparently from the same as H1865 (דְּרוֹר);
properly, a pearl (from its sheen as rapidly turned); by analogy, pearl-stone, i.e. mother-of-pearl or alabaster
KJV: [idiom] white.

H1859.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1755 (דּוֹר);
an age
KJV: generation.

H1860.definition:
or דֵּרָאוֹן; from an unused root (meaning to repulse);
an object of aversion
KJV: abhorring, contempt.

H1861.definition:
(also dor-bawn'); of uncertain derivation;
a goad
KJV: goad.

H1862.definition:
apparently from H1858 (דַּר) and H1843 (דֵּעַ); pearl of knowledge;
Darda, an Israelite
KJV: Darda.

H1863.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a thorn
KJV: thistle.

H1864.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
the south; poet. the south wind
KJV: south.

H1865.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to move rapidly);
freedom; hence, spontaneity of outflow, and so clear
KJV: liberty, pure.

H1866.definition:
the same as H1865 (דְּרוֹר), applied to a bird;
the swift, a kind of swallow
KJV: swallow.

H1867.definition:
of Persian origin;
Darejavesh, a title (rather than name) of several Persian kings
KJV: Darius.

H1868.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1867 (דָּֽרְיָוֵשׁ)
{Darejavesh, a title (rather than name) of several Persian kings}
KJV: Darius.

H1869.definition:
a primitive root;
to tread; by implication, to walk; also to string abow (by treading on it in bending)
KJV: archer, bend, come, draw, go (over), guide, lead (forth), thresh, tread (down), walk.

H1870.definition:
from H1869 (דָּרַךְ);
a road (as trodden); figuratively, a course of life or mode of action, often adverb
KJV: along, away, because of, [phrase] by, conversation, custom, (east-) ward, journey, manner, passenger, through, toward, (high-) (path-) way(-side), whither(-soever).

H1871.definition:
of Persian origin;
a 'drachma', or coin
KJV: dram.

H1872.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2220 (זְרוֹעַ);
an arm
KJV: arm.

H1873.definition:
probably a contraction from H1862 (דַּרְדַּע);
Dara, an Israelite
KJV: Dara.

H1874.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Darkon, one of 'Solomon's servants'
KJV: Darkon.

H1875.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to tread or frequent; usually to follow (for pursuit or search); by implication, to seek or ask; specifically to worship
KJV: ask, [idiom] at all, care for, [idiom] diligently, inquire, make inquisition, (necro-) mancer, question, require, search, seek (for, out), [idiom] surely.

H1876.definition:
a primitive root;
to sprout
KJV: bring forth, spring.

H1877.definition:
from H1876 (דָּשָׁא);
a sprout; by analogy, grass
KJV: (tender) grass, green, (tender) herb.

H1879.definition:
from H1878 (דָּשֵׁן);
fat; figuratively, rich, fertile
KJV: fat.

H1880.definition:
from H1878 (דָּשֵׁן);
the fat; abstractly fatness, i.e. (figuratively) abundance; specifically the (fatty) ashes of sacrifices
KJV: ashes, fatness.

H1881.definition:
of uncertain (perhaps foreign) derivation;
a royal edict or statute
KJV: commandment, commission, decree, law, manner.

H1882.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1881 (דָּת);
{a royal edict or statute}
KJV: decree, law.

H1883.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1877 (דֶּשֶׁא)
{a sprout; by analogy, grass}
KJV: tender grass.

H1884.definition:
(Aramaic) of Persian origin;
meaning one skilled in law; a judge
KJV: counsellor.

H1885.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Dathan, an Israelite
KJV: Dathan.

H1886.definition:
or (Aramaic dual) דֹּתַיִן; (Genesis 37:17), of uncertain derivation;
Dothan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Dothan. h

H1887.definition:
a primitive particle;
lo!
KJV: behold, lo.

H1888.definition:
(Aramaic) or הָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1887 (הֵא)
{lo!}
KJV: even, lo.

H1889.definition:
from H1887 (הֵא) and H253 (אָח);
aha!
KJV: ah, aha, ha.

H1890.definition:
by reduplication from H3051 (יָהַב);
gift (in sacrifice), i.e. holocaust
KJV: offering.

H1891.definition:
a primitive root;
to be vain in act, word, or expectation; specifically to lead astray
KJV: be (become, make) vain.

H1892.definition:
or (rarely in the abs.) הֲבֵל; from H1891 (הָבַל);
emptiness or vanity; figuratively, something transitory and unsatisfactory; often used as an adverb
KJV: [idiom] altogether, vain, vanity.

H1893.definition:
the same as H1892 (הֶבֶל);
Hebel, the son of Adam
KJV: Abel.

H1894.definition:
