ebony
KJV: ebony.

H1895.definition:
a primitive root of uncertain (perhaps foreign) derivation;
to be a horoscopist
KJV: [phrase] (astro-) loger.

H1896.definition:
or (by permutation) הֵגַי; probably of Persian origin;
Hege or Hegai, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Hegai, Hege.

H1897.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1901 (הָגִיג));
to murmur (in pleasure or anger); by implication, to ponder
KJV: imagine, meditate, mourn, mutter, roar, [idiom] sore, speak, study, talk, utter.

H1898.definition:
a primitive root;
to remove
KJV: stay, stay away.

H1899.definition:
from H1897 (הָגָה);
a muttering (in sighing, thought, or as thunder)
KJV: mourning, sound, tale.
